<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose to 1,406.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose to 1,406.</headline>
<text>
<p>LONDON, Feb 6 Reuter - The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,406 today from 1,387 on Feb 5, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p>  Route Index    Rate	Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1461    13.263	  1444    13.113</p>
<p>   1a   1454 11013.000	  1413 10700.000</p>
<p>   2    1732    24.738	  1719    24.563</p>
<p>   2a   1804 14794.000	  1757 14413.000</p>
<p>   3    1457    13.438	  1440    13.281</p>
<p>   3a   1429 11275.000	  1377 10869.000</p>
<p>   6    1253    12.925	  1253    12.925</p>
<p>   7    1212     5.900	  1221     5.944</p>
<p>   8     910    10.006	   915    10.056</p>
<p>   9     753  6581.000	   738  6450.000</p>
<p>  10    1140     5.756	  1140     5.756</p>
